  "latestMilestone": "Canonical SWIR_OS main now includes PR #50 at commit 3458bb94e8f39ec6ecd52e3d7eb44e82fac82a7e. System Edition gained a fail-closed fwupd/LVFS firmware transaction boundary with exact LVFS candidate binding, SHA-256 plan-digest confirmation, live metadata revalidation immediately before mutation, a private durable journal, explicit staged-reboot/recovery states and post-update fwupd history verification. Native Hardware Center can show bounded trusted LVFS candidates but exposes no mutation control. Automatic reboot/rollback, arbitrary firmware files/URLs and physical-hardware qualification remain disabled or unclaimed. PR #49 also expanded native Default Apps to browser, media, image and PDF handlers with real per-user Gio mutations. Authoritative roadmap progress remains 55/65 (84.6%); physical Live USB qualification and real-device firmware E2E remain pending.",
